        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under argon (Schlenk), a toluene solution of quinolinyl aminophenol H2L (0.74 g, 2.04 mmol) was slowly added to a stirred toluene solution of Yb[N(SiMe3)2]3 (1.33 g, 2.04 mmol) at room temperature. The mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 3 days to give a dark red solution. After a small amount of precipitate was removed by centrifugation, the clear solution was concentrated to about 8 mL. Dark red crystals of 1 formed on standing at room temperature for several days (0.71 g, 55% based on aminophenol).",
